You might be interested in this talk[0] by a WebKit engineer on how they&#x27;re implementing similar approaches using libTooling and their own smart pointer types.<p>For example, their tooling prevents code like this:<p><pre><code>    if (m_weakMember) { m_weakMember-&gt;doThing(); }
</code></pre>
from compiling, forcing you to explicitly create an owning local reference, like so:<p><pre><code>    if (RefPtr strongLocal = m_weakMember.get()) { strongLocal-&gt;doThing(); }
</code></pre>
unless it&#x27;s a trivial inlined function, like a simple getter.<p>[0]<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.youtube.com&#x2F;watch?v=RLw13wLM5Ko" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.youtube.com&#x2F;watch?v=RLw13wLM5Ko</a>
